1
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:53,600
Cao Jin.

2
00:00:55,280 --> 00:00:56,880
You did a great job on this.

3
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,000
By solving this case,

4
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:02,640
you've lived up to your uniform

5
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:05,319
and the title of a people's police officer.

6
00:01:05,319 --> 00:01:06,160
Great.

7
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:08,440
Now,

8
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,880
all of us

9
00:01:10,160 --> 00:01:12,520
can have a peaceful New Year.

10
00:01:14,120 --> 00:01:14,760
Chief.

11
00:01:15,240 --> 00:01:16,440
After the New Year,

12
00:01:16,920 --> 00:01:19,120
I want to apply to reopen the investigation

13
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,680
into the explosion at Zhao Zhiguo's house

14
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:21,720
sixteen years ago.

15
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:22,720
That case

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,730
was already ruled an accident.

17
00:01:24,880 --> 00:01:27,240
It was an explosion caused by a gas leak.

18
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:29,480
It's written clearly in the file.

19
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:31,360
Chief.

20
00:01:31,720 --> 00:01:33,720
Teng Xiaohu is currently on the run.

21
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:36,120
When we were arresting Teng Laohu that day,

22
00:01:36,200 --> 00:01:38,000
we heard him talking to someone.

23
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,400
He mentioned the explosion from back then.

24
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:41,880
His tone was very suspicious.

25
00:01:41,880 --> 00:01:43,539
I suspect he knows something.

26
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:44,880
I know.

27
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:47,640
You've always been obsessed with your father's death

28
00:01:47,640 --> 00:01:49,960
and the case from back then.

29
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:53,479
But we don't have any conclusive evidence.

30
00:01:53,479 --> 00:01:56,600
Relying solely on a suspect's

31
00:01:56,600 --> 00:01:58,720
vague remarks

32
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:01,800
to reopen a case that was ruled

33
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,730
as an accident over a decade ago...

34
00:02:03,840 --> 00:02:05,080
It's illogical.

35
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,120
Chief.

36
00:02:13,600 --> 00:02:14,460
How about this.

37
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:16,680
If after the New Year,

38
00:02:16,840 --> 00:02:18,040
we catch Teng Xiaohu,

39
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:21,000
or you have new clues

40
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,120
and solid evidence,

41
00:02:22,120 --> 00:02:23,579
we'll discuss this again.

42
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:27,200
What we need to do now is to completely close

43
00:02:27,360 --> 00:02:28,560
the case at hand.

44
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,760
Let everyone catch their breath,

45
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,760
and let yourself catch your breath,

46
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,240
so everyone can have a peaceful New Year.

47
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:08,000
Eat up, everyone.

48
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,160
Third Uncle, Third Aunt,

49
00:03:09,160 --> 00:03:10,640
you like shrimp, so let's put it over there.

50
00:03:10,640 --> 00:03:11,400
Come, come,

51
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,160
let's swap.

52
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:14,280
After the New Year,

53
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:15,880
I want to go back to the cabin.

54
00:03:16,840 --> 00:03:18,040
Then I'll go with you.

55
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,320
Have some dumplings.

56
00:03:55,520 --> 00:03:57,320
How can a pair of sevens beat a pair of twos?

57
00:03:57,320 --> 00:03:58,400
Right, right, right.

58
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,530
Right, take it back.

59
00:04:00,520 --> 00:04:01,400
Pair of tens.

60
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:03,880
Pair of jacks.

61
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:04,640
Bomb.

62
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:13,520
I'll give you a piece of candy, okay?

63
00:04:20,640 --> 00:04:21,399
Is it good?

64
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:29,240
Brother.

65
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:32,050
Why are you here?

66
00:04:32,920 --> 00:04:34,120
Brought this for you.

67
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:36,159
How is it?

68
00:04:38,040 --> 00:04:39,300
Did Auntie make these?

69
00:04:39,440 --> 00:04:40,900
I haven't tasted them yet.

70
00:04:51,280 --> 00:04:52,610
Do you want some garlic?

71
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,810
I forgot to bring it.

72
00:04:57,560 --> 00:04:58,920
They taste quite like

73
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,040
the ones my mom makes.

74
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:55,040
Mr. Wang.

75
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:56,800
If...

76
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:02,600
If anything happens to me,

77
00:06:04,600 --> 00:06:06,130
please take care of my Nian.

78
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,700
I'll finish mine. Drink at your own pace.

79
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,280
My mom went to the forestry center to find work.

80
00:07:17,280 --> 00:07:19,360
From now on, we can live a stable life.

81
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,690
The case of Zhiguo's family

82
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,460
is settled.

83
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:26,000
The gas cylinder explosion

84
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:26,930
was an accident.

85
00:07:28,640 --> 00:07:29,840
What about Xiaolong?

86
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:32,159
Yeah, such a young child

87
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:33,520
lost his parents.

88
00:07:33,840 --> 00:07:35,300
It's really tough for him.

89
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:36,640
I think,

90
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:39,000
even though my salary isn't much,

91
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:40,880
and an extra person means an extra mouth to feed,

92
00:07:40,880 --> 00:07:42,880
we should still adopt this child.

93
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:45,140
So I wanted to discuss it with you.

94
00:07:45,320 --> 00:07:46,360
When spring comes,

95
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:48,400
I'll find a job at the forestry center.

96
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:50,400
Xiaopao has grown up too, hasn't he?

97
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:51,560
It'll be fine.

98
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,730
Well, it'll be hard on you then.

99
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,280
Xiaopao,

100
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,640
I'm leaving.

101
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,400
W-Where are you going?

102
00:08:04,040 --> 00:08:06,280
I can't cause trouble for Uncle and Aunt.

103
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:07,480
I'm already fifteen.

104
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,160
My dad said

105
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:11,200
I'm already an adult.

106
00:08:12,480 --> 00:08:13,320
After I leave,

107
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:15,600
you must do your homework properly.

108
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:16,530
Don't run around

109
00:08:16,640 --> 00:08:17,770
and make Aunt worry.

110
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:21,280
C-Can you not leave?

111
00:08:28,280 --> 00:08:29,240
Take this.

112
00:08:32,679 --> 00:08:34,480
After I find out what happened to my family,

113
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,559
I will come back.

114
00:08:44,159 --> 00:08:44,800
Brother,

115
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,050
I'll be right here waiting for you.

116
00:09:00,400 --> 00:09:03,200
The snow was still heavy the last time we came here.

117
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:08,240
Wait for me outside.

118
00:09:09,080 --> 00:09:10,810
I'll go in and take a look first.

119
00:09:12,080 --> 00:09:13,140
Let's go together.

120
00:09:39,800 --> 00:09:40,920
These wooden boards

121
00:09:40,920 --> 00:09:42,800
look like they were pieced together later.

122
00:09:42,800 --> 00:09:44,460
Let's take them apart and see.

123
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:06,320
What's wrong?

124
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:12,640
What should we do?

125
00:10:12,800 --> 00:10:13,680
Do we have to...

126
00:10:15,880 --> 00:10:16,940
I'll go take a look.

127
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:33,440
Wang Hong.

128
00:10:40,320 --> 00:10:40,640
Fei.

129
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,240
My mom must have carved this.

130
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:49,160
My mom must have lived here.

131
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:50,800
Wang Hong.

132
00:10:50,920 --> 00:10:53,320
My mom must have stayed here for a long time.

133
00:10:54,960 --> 00:10:56,220
I'll call Officer Cao.

134
00:11:10,880 --> 00:11:11,640
Wang Hong.

135
00:11:11,920 --> 00:11:13,050
Hello, Officer Cao.

136
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:16,340
Inside the cabin in the primeval forest,

137
00:11:16,360 --> 00:11:17,960
we found Teng Xiaohu's body.

138
00:11:18,040 --> 00:11:19,080
Where exactly?

139
00:11:19,360 --> 00:11:21,120
In the cabin in the primeval forest.

140
00:11:21,120 --> 00:11:22,280
We'll wait for you at the entrance.

141
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:23,640
Okay, I'm on my way.

142
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:24,320
Xiao Ma.

143
00:11:24,800 --> 00:11:26,040
We have a crime scene, a homicide.

144
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:26,970
Call forensics.

145
00:11:27,320 --> 00:11:28,680
Primeval forest, homicide.

146
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:29,080
Hurry up.

147
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:29,680
Homicide.

148
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,160
Are all the procedures done?

149
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,040
They're done. Don't worry.

150
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,360
The doctor said

151
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,560
you need to rest now.

152
00:11:42,560 --> 00:11:43,960
Stop worrying.

153
00:11:45,640 --> 00:11:47,440
I'll feel at ease once it's done.

154
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,880
How can I not worry?

155
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,640
I know my own body.

156
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:56,000
I don't have many days left.

157
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:57,760
Don't talk nonsense.

158
00:11:58,480 --> 00:11:59,680
It's not nonsense.

159
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:00,880
You see,

160
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,760
life

161
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,320
is like taking a bus,

162
00:12:05,080 --> 00:12:07,200
stop by stop.

163
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,570
There's a lot of scenery along the way,

164
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:13,400
mountains, lakes, and forests,

165
00:12:13,400 --> 00:12:15,130
and tall buildings in the city.

166
00:12:17,920 --> 00:12:19,200
Once you get on the bus,

167
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:21,840
you meet many different people and things.

168
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:25,600
It's quite interesting to think about.

169
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,480
But no matter who you are,

170
00:12:28,400 --> 00:12:31,240
you have to get off at the terminal.

171
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,840
I've been

172
00:12:36,560 --> 00:12:38,120
calculating my whole life,

173
00:12:38,880 --> 00:12:39,680
just wanting

174
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:42,360
to make my factory bigger and stronger.

175
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:46,560
It's inevitable to make some mistakes.

176
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:47,800
In the end,

177
00:12:48,560 --> 00:12:49,440
I just want

178
00:12:49,920 --> 00:12:51,980
to do one thing without calculating.

179
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,840
I think I can do it.

180
00:12:57,280 --> 00:12:57,880
Also,

181
00:12:58,920 --> 00:12:59,880
at home,

182
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:03,000
in the safe next to it,

183
00:13:03,120 --> 00:13:05,480
in the hidden compartment on the second floor,

184
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:06,880
there are two bankbooks.

185
00:13:07,680 --> 00:13:09,000
It's my life savings.

186
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:09,920
I'm giving it all to you.

187
00:13:09,920 --> 00:13:10,920
I don't want it.

188
00:13:11,800 --> 00:13:13,080
How can you not want it?

189
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:14,480
How will you live if you don't take it?

190
00:13:14,480 --> 00:13:15,400
Listen to me.

191
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,480
After I'm gone,

192
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,480
just forget about me.

193
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,960
Find a sincere and reliable person

194
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:26,520
and live a good life.

195
00:13:35,840 --> 00:13:36,840
I'm just kidding.

196
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,290
Don't overthink it.

197
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:40,080
Stop peeling that.

198
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:41,720
I can't eat.

199
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:43,050
I just want to take a nap.

200
00:13:47,800 --> 00:13:48,880
I want some water.

201
00:14:01,560 --> 00:14:03,240
Don't worry about me. Take a rest.

202
00:14:03,240 --> 00:14:04,300
I want to take a nap.

203
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:27,520
What is this that you have to write right now?

204
00:14:27,520 --> 00:14:28,720
You're coughing so badly.

205
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:29,440
Okay.

206
00:14:29,800 --> 00:14:30,860
I'll listen to you.

207
00:14:30,880 --> 00:14:31,940
I'll stop writing.

208
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,080
Come on.

209
00:14:38,440 --> 00:14:39,120
Lie down.

210
00:14:39,600 --> 00:14:40,880
I can't sleep well.

211
00:14:40,880 --> 00:14:42,010
I can't fall asleep.

212
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:44,120
Hold me while I sleep.

213
00:15:04,400 --> 00:15:05,600
I'm almost done here.

214
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:08,840
The deceased has obvious strangulation marks on the neck.

215
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,840
And blunt force trauma to the head.

216
00:15:11,280 --> 00:15:13,680
The cause of death is mechanical asphyxia.

217
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,920
The time of death was likely five days ago.

218
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:16,960
For the rest,

219
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,820
I have to go back and do an autopsy.

220
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:23,480
This is not the primary crime scene.

221
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,360
There are no signs of a struggle.

222
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,560
His body

223
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:31,720
was moved here from somewhere else.

224
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:47,890
Brother.

225
00:15:53,200 --> 00:15:54,160
At first glance,

226
00:15:54,320 --> 00:15:56,840
someone was imprisoned here for a long time.

227
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,400
These scratch marks

228
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:02,060
were likely made by the person imprisoned here.

229
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,480
Look at this.

230
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:06,680
Here and on the ground,

231
00:16:06,680 --> 00:16:08,410
there are some friction marks.

232
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:12,700
They were likely caused by someone sitting and lying down for a long time.

233
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:24,640
Feifei.
